{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784301821,"nonce":"UNDwCRWOqILWZbmJhsgnCtapfRU=","title":"[dogfood] forge set_status failures are silent — stuck outbox, no log, no metric","message":"drain_forge_statuses (server lib.rs ~2157) posts commit statuses and only mark_dispatched on success: `if forge.set_status(...).await.is_ok()`. A failing post is left for redelivery — correct for at-least-once, but the Err is DROPPED: no log line, no metric, no dead-letter after N attempts. \n\nDuring dogfood, every trigger run's status was stuck (9 undispatched run_status_changed rows, delivery_attempts stayed 0) and NOTHING surfaced why. Only by minting a token by hand did I find the real cause: HTTP 403 'Resource not accessible by integration' (App lacks statuses:write). \n\nTwo things worth fixing:\n1. Observability: log set_status failures (at warn) with the forge error + response, and/or increment delivery_attempts + dead-letter after a cap, so a misconfigured install is diagnosable from logs instead of a manual token mint.\n2. The claimed rows show delivery_attempts=0 despite repeated re-claims — the attempt counter is not incremented on this path, so dead-lettering (if any) can never trigger.\n\n(The underlying 403 is an App-permission setup gap, tracked separately — but the silent-swallow is a Scarab observability bug.)","files":null}]}